==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*atro-ek}}, from {{m|ine-pro||*h₂eh₁tro-h₃kʷs|having the appearance of fire}}, from {{m|ine-pro||*h₂eh₁tro-}} (suffixed, metathesized form of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eh₁ter-||fire}}) + {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-||eye; to see}}. The first root also gives the cognates of {{cog|ae|𐬁𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬱||fire}}, {{cog|xum||tr=atru|sc=Ital}}, {{cog|osc||tr=Aadíriis|sc=Ital}}, {{cog|ga|áith||kiln}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈa.troːks/|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-3rd-1E|atrōx|atrōcis}}

# [[fierce]], [[savage]], [[bloody]]
# [[heinous]], [[cruel]], [[severe]]
# [[terrible]], [[frightening]], [[dreadful]]

